# oracle: RHEO 2d fluid with two atom types of different viscosity and conductivity, pair_style rheo with harmonic/means (the viscosity and the thermal diffusivity of each pair are harmonic means instead of arithmetic ones), atom_style rheo/thermal, fix rheo thermal, fix rheo/viscosity per type, fix rheo/thermal conductivity per type, fix rheo/pressure, nve and enforce2d
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box), engine vs native: the per-atom x, v and f agree to 2e-16 (scaled by max(1, |value|)) and the thermo ke to 1e-16 relative over the 40 steps. With the arithmetic means of the same input (harmonic/means removed) the velocities after 40 steps differ by 0.059 and the forces by 0.072, so the case tells the two averages apart.
units        lj
dimension    2
atom_style   rheo/thermal
boundary     p p p
comm_modify  vel yes
newton       off
region       box block 0 5 0 5 -0.01 0.01
create_box   2 box
lattice      sq 0.9
create_atoms 1 box
mass         * 1.0
region       hot block 0 2.5 0 2.5 -1 1
set          region hot type 2
set          group all rheo/rho 1.0
set          group all rheo/status 0
set          group all sph/e 0.5
set          region hot sph/e 2.0
velocity     all create 0.3 4928459 dist uniform units box
timestep     0.005
pair_style   rheo 3.0 harmonic/means
pair_coeff   * *
fix          1 all rheo 3.0 quintic 0 thermal
fix          2 all rheo/viscosity 1 constant 0.05 2 constant 0.4
fix          3 all rheo/pressure * linear
fix          4 all rheo/thermal conductivity 1 constant 0.1 conductivity 2 constant 0.02 specific/heat * constant 1.0
fix          5 all enforce2d
fix          6 all nve
thermo       10
thermo_style custom step ke pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run          40
